```typescript
import { Bash } from "just-bash";

const bash = new Bash();
await bash.exec('echo "Hello" > greeting.txt');
const result = await bash.exec("cat greeting.txt");
console.log(result.stdout); // "Hello\n"
console.log(result.exitCode); // 0
```

Each `exec()` call gets its own isolated shell state — environment variables, functions, and working directory reset between calls. The **filesystem is shared** across calls, so files written in one `exec()`...
